	quest.6D84FDAF0985446B.quest_desc: ["Interrupt one fusion craft or drain one high-energy buffer and verify ingredient recovery and containment-safe restart.","Acceptance: the failure remains local, no rare input is voided, the reason is visible and the system can be made safe without destroying healthy sections."]
	quest.7F705B66BEEC5323.title: "14. Draconic Engineering — Automation Proof"
	quest.7F705B66BEEC5323.quest_desc: ["Automate repeatable injectors and components while keeping awakening, unique boss proof and dangerous reactor controls explicit.","Acceptance: run the system unattended for a representative batch, then show that empty input, full output and chunk reload do not create duplication or deadlock."]
	quest.2BF000216C70D195.title: "14. Draconic Engineering — Anti-Bypass Audit"
	quest.2BF000216C70D195.quest_desc: ["Close Wyvern, awakened core, modules, equipment and Chaos materials across loot, rewards, EMC, resource generators and alternate fusion recipes.","Acceptance: every gated output has one authoritative path or explicitly equivalent paths, zero unauthorized rewards and an explicit policy for EMC, loot, trade and resource simulation."]
	quest.3E59E22E59869C60.title: "14. Draconic Engineering — Recovery and Repeatability"
	quest.3E59E22E59869C60.quest_desc: ["Restore fusion and energy containment after a simulated injector or transfer failure using spare components and recorded configuration.","Acceptance: recovery uses stored ordinary spares and documented state, not administrator commands, creative items or a second copy of a unique permission."]
	quest.F6E9886FDD82A0AE.title: "14. Draconic Engineering — Stage Acceptance"
	quest.F6E9886FDD82A0AE.quest_desc: ["Produce and retain the milestone kubejs:draconic_processor after completing supply, process, integration, measurement, failure, automation, bypass and recovery checks for Draconic Engineering.","The milestone proves infrastructure once; it must not become a repeated manual tax. Keep the factory capable of reproducing ordinary consumed components before entering the next stage."]
	quest.3786800D2223B541.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Entry Contract"
	quest.3786800D2223B541.quest_desc: ["Stage 15 — Contained Transmutation begins only after the previous milestone is complete. The required domains are projecte, extendedcrafting, draconicevolution; none is decorative in the main route.","Before building new machinery, list the legal inputs, the three most important gated outputs (projecte:philosophers_stone, projecte:transmutation_table, kubejs:transmutation_matrix) and the condition that would make the stage unsafe or premature."]
	quest.B478FA4BFD813902.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Supply Contract"
	quest.B478FA4BFD813902.quest_desc: ["Maintain tracked matter tiers, catalysts, draconic components, ultimate crafting parts and an explicit list of zero-EMC progression items.","Acceptance: inputs have labelled source, minimum and maximum stock, overflow destination and a replacement route that does not depend on a random reward."]
	quest.E947A40BAA85C8AF.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Core Process"
	quest.E947A40BAA85C8AF.quest_desc: ["Build EMC acquisition, matter compression and controlled transmutation access as audited systems with no hidden positive loops.","Acceptance: complete three representative cycles, account for every consumed input and returned container or tool, and identify the slowest operation."]
	quest.86F7FF2070D89E72.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Cross-Mod Interface"
	quest.86F7FF2070D89E72.quest_desc: ["Use ProjectE only after Extended Crafting and Draconic infrastructure prove that transmutation accelerates mature production rather than replacing progression.","Acceptance: document exactly which mod owns each transformation, which buffer separates them and why no circular or later-stage dependency exists."]
	quest.A64339A03740EBBC.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Measurement and Buffers"
	quest.A64339A03740EBBC.quest_desc: ["Record EMC input and output, non-EMC exceptions, matter conversion loss or gain and the effect of automation on each controlled resource.","Acceptance: write the measured values in the quest notes or an in-game clipboard and size buffers from observed rates rather than guesswork."]
	quest.A9ACF205EF7ECEAA.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Controlled Failure Test"
	quest.A9ACF205EF7ECEAA.quest_desc: ["Remove access to the transmutation table and prove that the factory can still produce repair parts and restore the system without EMC deadlock.","Acceptance: the failure remains local, no rare input is voided, the reason is visible and the system can be made safe without destroying healthy sections."]
	quest.97CD66C8B744B671.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Automation Proof"
	quest.97CD66C8B744B671.quest_desc: ["Automate only allowlisted bulk conversion with bounded requests, protected reserve and explicit cancellation of runaway jobs.","Acceptance: run the system unattended for a representative batch, then show that empty input, full output and chunk reload do not create duplication or deadlock."]
	quest.D5403BBD6AEE56A4.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Anti-Bypass Audit"
	quest.D5403BBD6AEE56A4.quest_desc: ["Audit every gated item against custom EMC, tome learning, tablet access, loot, rewards, trades, condensers and addon conversion recipes.","Acceptance: every gated output has one authoritative path or explicitly equivalent paths, zero unauthorized rewards and an explicit policy for EMC, loot, trade and resource simulation."]
	quest.AC711C249673FCF6.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Recovery and Repeatability"
	quest.AC711C249673FCF6.quest_desc: ["Rebuild the EMC network from a documented non-EMC recovery cache and verify all blacklisted entries remain zero after restart.","Acceptance: recovery uses stored ordinary spares and documented state, not administrator commands, creative items or a second copy of a unique permission."]
	quest.6E6218D68A91581C.title: "15. Contained Transmutation — Stage Acceptance"
	quest.6E6218D68A91581C.quest_desc: ["Produce and retain the milestone kubejs:transmutation_matrix after completing supply, process, integration, measurement, failure, automation, bypass and recovery checks for Contained Transmutation.","The milestone proves infrastructure once; it must not become a repeated manual tax. Keep the factory capable of reproducing ordinary consumed components before entering the next stage."]
	quest.715E91E91FA04750.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Entry Contract"
	quest.715E91E91FA04750.quest_desc: ["Stage 16 — Extreme Fabrication begins only after the previous milestone is complete. The required domains are extendedcrafting, avaritia, projecte; none is decorative in the main route.","Before building new machinery, list the legal inputs, the three most important gated outputs (extendedcrafting:ultimate_table, avaritia:extreme_crafting_table, kubejs:cosmic_catalyst) and the condition that would make the stage unsafe or premature."]
	quest.2F62BCC4841FD480.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Supply Contract"
	quest.2F62BCC4841FD480.quest_desc: ["Maintain ultimate crafting components, catalysts, singularity materials, extreme tables and parallel resource lines with bounded buffers.","Acceptance: inputs have labelled source, minimum and maximum stock, overflow destination and a replacement route that does not depend on a random reward."]
	quest.1137FE372EC2E261.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Core Process"
	quest.1137FE372EC2E261.quest_desc: ["Automate large-pattern crafting, singularity compression and extreme component assembly as scalable factory operations.","Acceptance: complete three representative cycles, account for every consumed input and returned container or tool, and identify the slowest operation."]
	quest.CAB85D1360D9D498.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Cross-Mod Interface"
	quest.CAB85D1360D9D498.quest_desc: ["Converge Extended Crafting, Avaritia and ProjectE only through authoritative outputs from earlier automated domains.","Acceptance: document exactly which mod owns each transformation, which buffer separates them and why no circular or later-stage dependency exists."]
	quest.9E3471DA1BA18003.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Measurement and Buffers"
	quest.9E3471DA1BA18003.quest_desc: ["Record resource rate per singularity, craft duration, table occupancy, catalyst return, parallel capacity and the dominant bottleneck.","Acceptance: write the measured values in the quest notes or an in-game clipboard and size buffers from observed rates rather than guesswork."]
	quest.AD865EE3F2259837.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Controlled Failure Test"
	quest.AD865EE3F2259837.quest_desc: ["Interrupt one large craft and verify all rare inputs remain accounted for and can resume without manual recipe reconstruction.","Acceptance: the failure remains local, no rare input is voided, the reason is visible and the system can be made safe without destroying healthy sections."]
	quest.3FBDAA28936802C8.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Automation Proof"
	quest.3FBDAA28936802C8.quest_desc: ["Use request limits and stage-specific stock targets so extreme fabrication scales infrastructure rather than repetitive clicking.","Acceptance: run the system unattended for a representative batch, then show that empty input, full output and chunk reload do not create duplication or deadlock."]
	quest.1F991A0241A1194E.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Anti-Bypass Audit"
	quest.1F991A0241A1194E.quest_desc: ["Close ultimate tables, extreme tables, singularities and catalysts through loot, rewards, EMC, seed or bee production, salvage and addon crafters.","Acceptance: every gated output has one authoritative path or explicitly equivalent paths, zero unauthorized rewards and an explicit policy for EMC, loot, trade and resource simulation."]
	quest.731EDD778037D501.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Recovery and Repeatability"
	quest.731EDD778037D501.quest_desc: ["Restore an interrupted singularity and large-craft pipeline from stored intermediate components and recorded request state.","Acceptance: recovery uses stored ordinary spares and documented state, not administrator commands, creative items or a second copy of a unique permission."]
	quest.F73DBC61E72AB52A.title: "16. Extreme Fabrication — Stage Acceptance"
	quest.F73DBC61E72AB52A.quest_desc: ["Produce and retain the milestone kubejs:cosmic_catalyst after completing supply, process, integration, measurement, failure, automation, bypass and recovery checks for Extreme Fabrication.","The milestone proves infrastructure once; it must not become a repeated manual tax. Keep the factory capable of reproducing ordinary consumed components before entering the next stage."]
	quest.A7A7D239EF747E58.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Entry Contract"
	quest.A7A7D239EF747E58.quest_desc: ["Stage 17 — Cosmic Synthesis begins only after the previous milestone is complete. The required domains are avaritia, draconicevolution, divinerpg, stellaris; none is decorative in the main route.","Before building new machinery, list the legal inputs, the three most important gated outputs (kubejs:cosmic_synthesis_core, avaritia:infinity_ingot) and the condition that would make the stage unsafe or premature."]
	quest.404270DAE20A2FD1.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Supply Contract"
	quest.404270DAE20A2FD1.quest_desc: ["Maintain Infinity catalysts, awakened cores, antimatter controls, stellar or dimensional resources and reusable lunar permissions in separate vaults.","Acceptance: inputs have labelled source, minimum and maximum stock, overflow destination and a replacement route that does not depend on a random reward."]
	quest.58497FDAD750C4A1.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Core Process"
	quest.58497FDAD750C4A1.quest_desc: ["Build Infinity-material, stellar-resource and cosmic-energy production as converging supply chains with no single random bottleneck.","Acceptance: complete three representative cycles, account for every consumed input and returned container or tool, and identify the slowest operation."]
	quest.147509E401C3D8B5.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Cross-Mod Interface"
	quest.147509E401C3D8B5.quest_desc: ["Combine Avaritia, Draconic Evolution, DivineRPG and stellar content while preserving real first victories and scalable ordinary materials.","Acceptance: document exactly which mod owns each transformation, which buffer separates them and why no circular or later-stage dependency exists."]
	quest.E74686C3AE1AB4AE.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Measurement and Buffers"
	quest.E74686C3AE1AB4AE.quest_desc: ["Record production time and bottleneck for one Infinity Ingot, energy reserve, unique permissions used and repeatable bulk inputs.","Acceptance: write the measured values in the quest notes or an in-game clipboard and size buffers from observed rates rather than guesswork."]
	quest.0CC8F113ACB87FDB.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Controlled Failure Test"
	quest.0CC8F113ACB87FDB.quest_desc: ["Remove one cosmic input line and prove the remaining factory stops safely without consuming irreplaceable catalysts or permissions.","Acceptance: the failure remains local, no rare input is voided, the reason is visible and the system can be made safe without destroying healthy sections."]
	quest.4C336F5BFF730965.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Automation Proof"
	quest.4C336F5BFF730965.quest_desc: ["Automate ordinary cosmic components and material convergence while keeping unique encounter evidence reusable but non-generatable.","Acceptance: run the system unattended for a representative batch, then show that empty input, full output and chunk reload do not create duplication or deadlock."]
	quest.6133257BF97F28D7.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Anti-Bypass Audit"
	quest.6133257BF97F28D7.quest_desc: ["Audit Infinity materials, stellar drops and cosmic catalysts across EMC, loot, rewards, trades, simulation, seeds, bees and creative-item recipes.","Acceptance: every gated output has one authoritative path or explicitly equivalent paths, zero unauthorized rewards and an explicit policy for EMC, loot, trade and resource simulation."]
	quest.7ECCCACE8EE71D54.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Recovery and Repeatability"
	quest.7ECCCACE8EE71D54.quest_desc: ["Resume cosmic synthesis after one supply-chain outage using protected intermediates and a written order of reconnection.","Acceptance: recovery uses stored ordinary spares and documented state, not administrator commands, creative items or a second copy of a unique permission."]
	quest.20A0D864E9A9EB7E.title: "17. Cosmic Synthesis — Stage Acceptance"
	quest.20A0D864E9A9EB7E.quest_desc: ["Produce and retain the milestone kubejs:cosmic_synthesis_core after completing supply, process, integration, measurement, failure, automation, bypass and recovery checks for Cosmic Synthesis.","The milestone proves infrastructure once; it must not become a repeated manual tax. Keep the factory capable of reproducing ordinary consumed components before entering the next stage."]
	quest.8782D5658C1ED20A.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Entry Contract"
	quest.8782D5658C1ED20A.quest_desc: ["Stage 18 — Creative Convergence begins only after the previous milestone is complete. The required domains are avaritia, extendedcrafting, projecte, mekanism, ae2; none is decorative in the main route.","Before building new machinery, list the legal inputs, the three most important gated outputs (kubejs:creative_convergence_matrix) and the condition that would make the stage unsafe or premature."]
	quest.7F2B7BD2AD47B71F.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Supply Contract"
	quest.7F2B7BD2AD47B71F.quest_desc: ["Maintain audited creative components, Infinity materials, antimatter, quantum logic, singularities and completion proofs in isolated final stores.","Acceptance: inputs have labelled source, minimum and maximum stock, overflow destination and a replacement route that does not depend on a random reward."]
	quest.C2650E8BC29E53FB.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Core Process"
	quest.C2650E8BC29E53FB.quest_desc: ["Assemble creative convergence only from completed automated domains and documented mastery projects, never from raw manual stockpiles alone.","Acceptance: complete three representative cycles, account for every consumed input and returned container or tool, and identify the slowest operation."]
	quest.A3264536DE87E12C.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Cross-Mod Interface"
	quest.A3264536DE87E12C.quest_desc: ["Require Avaritia, Extended Crafting, ProjectE, Mekanism and AE2 final infrastructure to cooperate without creating an infinite positive loop before completion.","Acceptance: document exactly which mod owns each transformation, which buffer separates them and why no circular or later-stage dependency exists."]
	quest.62B0A0009FAEAE9C.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Measurement and Buffers"
	quest.62B0A0009FAEAE9C.quest_desc: ["Record every final input, its authoritative source, production time, energy or EMC cost, reusable proof and remaining bottleneck.","Acceptance: write the measured values in the quest notes or an in-game clipboard and size buffers from observed rates rather than guesswork."]
	quest.36E0BD1A31AFA2EF.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Controlled Failure Test"
	quest.36E0BD1A31AFA2EF.quest_desc: ["Abort the final assembly before completion and verify that rare inputs, permissions and completion state remain recoverable and unduplicated.","Acceptance: the failure remains local, no rare input is voided, the reason is visible and the system can be made safe without destroying healthy sections."]
	quest.0F4822AB00418AB1.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Automation Proof"
	quest.0F4822AB00418AB1.quest_desc: ["Automate final requests with hard one-craft limits, protected reserves and human-visible confirmation before any rule-altering output.","Acceptance: run the system unattended for a representative batch, then show that empty input, full output and chunk reload do not create duplication or deadlock."]
	quest.10384D9BEB08C13B.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Anti-Bypass Audit"
	quest.10384D9BEB08C13B.quest_desc: ["Perform a complete audit of recipes, rewards, loot, EMC, trades, simulation, resource generation, uncrafting and creative-item addons for every final input.","Acceptance: every gated output has one authoritative path or explicitly equivalent paths, zero unauthorized rewards and an explicit policy for EMC, loot, trade and resource simulation."]
	quest.F7E0B19DB664A2EA.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Recovery and Repeatability"
	quest.F7E0B19DB664A2EA.quest_desc: ["Reopen the world, repeat the final audit and prove that completion remains valid without duplicate rewards or lost quest state.","Acceptance: recovery uses stored ordinary spares and documented state, not administrator commands, creative items or a second copy of a unique permission."]
	quest.9197E9880C695F53.title: "18. Creative Convergence — Stage Acceptance"
	quest.9197E9880C695F53.quest_desc: ["Produce and retain the milestone kubejs:creative_convergence_matrix after completing supply, process, integration, measurement, failure, automation, bypass and recovery checks for Creative Convergence.","The milestone proves infrastructure once; it must not become a repeated manual tax. Keep the factory capable of reproducing ordinary consumed components before entering the next stage."]
	chapter.82BA177C4B4DBFBB.title: "Expert Progression Spine — 18 Stages / 72 Substages"
	quest.B9B6DA53582B39E3.title: "Field Foundations — Survival Workshop: System Contract"
	quest.B9B6DA53582B39E3.quest_desc: ["Stage 1 — Field Foundations: Survival Workshop defines part of the mandatory route toward kubejs:field_engineering_kit. This stage joins minecraft, immersiveengineering, actuallyadditions and focuses on recoverable manual work, early material identity and survival safety before automation.","Study the system before building it: identify inputs, outputs, constraints, ownership, repeatability and recovery; list legal inputs, controlled outputs and failure boundaries, and explain why the substage belongs before the gated outputs kubejs:field_engineering_kit, kubejs:materials_analysis_matrix, kubejs:power_regulation_unit."]
	quest.8E184D5D32457E38.title: "Field Foundations — Survival Workshop: Infrastructure Build"
	quest.8E184D5D32457E38.quest_desc: ["Build a bounded demonstration of Survival Workshop using at least two stage domains from minecraft, immersiveengineering, actuallyadditions. Assign every input, output, buffer, reusable component and control signal to an explicit owner.","The design must address inputs, outputs, constraints, ownership, repeatability and recovery. Prefer repeatable infrastructure over manual repetition, include a visible stop condition and leave enough access to replace one failed component without dismantling unrelated production."]
	quest.8E5140546221324A.title: "Field Foundations — Survival Workshop: Production Acceptance"
	quest.8E5140546221324A.quest_desc: ["Accept the Survival Workshop installation as a production system, not as a placed-block checklist. Run a representative cycle and record manual batch time, spare tools, protected storage and recovery after a simulated loss.","Test full output, missing input and interrupted power or transport; recover without duplication or loss, review rewards, EMC, loot, trade, simulation and alternate recipes, and confirm that progression advances only through the declared milestone kubejs:field_engineering_kit."]
	quest.2F05EA409AC0805C.title: "Field Foundations — Material Identification: System Contract"
	quest.2F05EA409AC0805C.quest_desc: ["Stage 1 — Field Foundations: Material Identification defines part of the mandatory route toward kubejs:field_engineering_kit. This stage joins minecraft, immersiveengineering, actuallyadditions and focuses on recoverable manual work, early material identity and survival safety before automation.","Study the system before building it: identify legal first sources, conversion yield, renewable limits and protected-material policy; list legal inputs, controlled outputs and failure boundaries, and explain why the substage belongs before the gated outputs kubejs:field_engineering_kit, kubejs:materials_analysis_matrix, kubejs:power_regulation_unit."]
	quest.01DF0222CC54FC98.title: "Field Foundations — Material Identification: Infrastructure Build"
	quest.01DF0222CC54FC98.quest_desc: ["Build a bounded demonstration of Material Identification using at least two stage domains from minecraft, immersiveengineering, actuallyadditions. Assign every input, output, buffer, reusable component and control signal to an explicit owner.","The design must address legal first sources, conversion yield, renewable limits and protected-material policy. Prefer repeatable infrastructure over manual repetition, include a visible stop condition and leave enough access to replace one failed component without dismantling unrelated production."]
	quest.48094892F0E4C37E.title: "Field Foundations — Material Identification: Production Acceptance"
	quest.48094892F0E4C37E.quest_desc: ["Accept the Material Identification installation as a production system, not as a placed-block checklist. Run a representative cycle and record manual batch time, spare tools, protected storage and recovery after a simulated loss.","Test full output, missing input and interrupted power or transport; recover without duplication or loss, review rewards, EMC, loot, trade, simulation and alternate recipes, and confirm that progression advances only through the declared milestone kubejs:field_engineering_kit."]
